body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Errors before running","With tests","Where required"],"captions":["A type checker catches a wrong type, access to a field of None and a forgotten result before running","Types document intent better than comments, since they are checked automatically; raise strictness gradually","Always annotate public library functions and module boundaries; small internal ones are optional"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["def area(w: float, h: float) -> float: ...","area('3', 4)   # error before running"],"hl":[1],"bad":[1],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":30.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"types","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"linter","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"tests","tone":"blue","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":116.0,"text":"together: more reliable","tone":"green","size":10.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"public API","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"always typed","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"small function","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"optional","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[14.5,26.2]}]},{"title":"pytest","sub":"Tests","short":"pytest","main":"Coverage is not proof.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["A test is a function","Arrange–Act–Assert","Parametrization","Coverage"],"captions":["pytest: a test is a plain function, a check is a plain assert, a failure shows subexpression values","Three parts: arrange, act, assert; fixtures build shared data","@pytest.mark.parametrize runs one test over a table of inputs: no copy and paste","Coverage shows which lines ran but does not prove correctness: aim for scenarios, not a number"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["def test_total():","    assert total([1, 2, 3]) == 6"],"hl":[1],"lang":"python","size":12.0,"lh":30.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def test_discount():","    cart = Cart([100])      # arrange","    cart.apply('10%')       # act","    assert cart.total == 90 # assert"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["@pytest.mark.parametrize('a, b, want', [","    (1, 2, 3), (0, 0, 0), (-1, 1, 0)])","def test_add(a, b, want):","    assert add(a, b) == want"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"coverage 100%","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"no asserts","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"lines ran, not checked","size":10.0}]],"cues":[12.9,17.3,25.1]}]},{"title":"Good tests","sub":"Behavior and determinism","short":"Good tests","main":"A test must not block refactoring.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Behavior, not implementation","Determinism","Mocks and properties"],"captions":["A test checks behavior: if renaming a private function breaks ten tests, they depend on the implementation","Replace time, randomness, network and files, or the test will be \"flaky\"","Mock records calls to an external service; property tests check a general rule over many random inputs"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"behavior","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"implementation ✗","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"tests do not block refactoring","size":10.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"time","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":160.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"random","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":250.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"network","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":332.0,"y":70.0,"w":52.0,"h":28.0,"text":"files","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"replaced: the test is stable","tone":"green","size":10.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["fetch = Mock(return_value='Anna')","assert greet(7, fetch) == 'Hello, Anna'","fetch.assert_called_once_with(7)","# property: sorted(xs) loses no elements"],"hl":[0,2],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.6,30.4]}]},{"title":"Documentation","sub":"Docstring and doctest","short":"Documentation","main":"A comment explains \"why\".","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Docstring","doctest","Comments"],"captions":["Docstrings describe purpose, parameters, result and errors; README says how to install and run","Docstring examples are checked by doctest: an outdated example becomes a failing test","A comment explains \"why\", not \"what\"; most valuable is a warning about a non-obvious limitation"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["def clamp(x, low, high):","    \"\"\"Clamps x to the range.","","    Raises: ValueError if low > high.","    \"\"\""],"hl":[1,3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["    >>> clamp(15, 0, 10)","    10","    >>> clamp(-3, 0, 10)","    0"],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":26.0,"w":330.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":140.0,"text":"python -m doctest module.py","tone":"green","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["x = x + 1        # increment x   ← useless","# API returns dates in UTC: no shift needed   ← useful"],"hl":[1],"bad":[0],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":32.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[15.1,23.9]}]},{"title":"Errors and logging","sub":"Exceptions and logging","short":"Errors and logging","main":"Own exception hierarchy, logging instead of print.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Own exceptions","logging","What to write"],"captions":["Don't swallow exceptions or catch everything; build a hierarchy: AppError and subclasses for specific cases","Use logging instead of print: levels, formats, handlers; detail is toggled without editing code","Message: what happened and with what data, no secrets; log at boundaries: inputs, external services, surprises"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":34.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"AppError","tone":"yellow","size":11.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":100.0,"y":100.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"NotFound","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":260.0,"y":100.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"ValidationError","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":150.0,"y1":48.0,"x2":120.0,"y2":88.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":48.0,"x2":240.0,"y2":88.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"code","id":"c~code","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["log = logging.getLogger('app')","log.info('order %s created', order_id)","log.warning('request retry: %s', url)","log.error('payment failure', exc_info=True)"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":56.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"what happened","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":96.0,"w":120.0,"h":26.0,"text":"with what data","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":270.0,"y":76.0,"w":120.0,"h":30.0,"text":"no secrets","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[18.8,28.6]}]},{"title":"Design principles","sub":"SRP, DIP, simplicity","short":"Principles","main":"Simple today beats complex for later.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["One responsibility","Depend on interfaces","Simplicity"],"captions":["Single responsibility: a function or class has one reason to change","Dependency inversion: high level depends on interfaces, not implementations; composition beats inheritance","Don't repeat yourself, but don't invent shared code early: two similar functions beat a premature abstraction; simple today beats complex for later"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":110.0,"h":30.0,"text":"reads","tone":"red","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":230.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"computes","tone":"red","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":330.0,"y":70.0,"w":56.0,"h":30.0,"text":"writes","tone":"red","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"one function: three reasons to change","size":10.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"application","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"interface","tone":"yellow","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":28.0,"text":"implementation","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":116.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":134.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":244.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":262.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"dash":"3 3","width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"two similar functions","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"shared abstraction","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"not needed until needed","size":10.5}]],"cues":[11.0,29.6]}]},{"title":"Design patterns","sub":"Shorter in Python","short":"Patterns","main":"Patterns are a shared team vocabulary.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Strategy and factory","Singleton and observer","Built in"],"captions":["Strategy is a function passed as a parameter; factory is a function or class method that creates an object","Singleton is a module-level object; observer is a list of callbacks; adapter is a thin wrapper over a foreign interface","Iterator and context manager are built in, decorator is syntax; patterns are a shared vocabulary with colleagues"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def apply(price, strategy):","    return strategy(price)","apply(100, lambda p: p * 0.9)","Shape.from_json(text)   # factory"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["config = Config()          # singleton: a module","handlers = []","def emit(e):","    for h in handlers: h(e)  # observer"],"hl":[3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":62.0,"y":56.0,"w":112.0,"h":26.0,"text":"iterator","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":192.0,"y":56.0,"w":112.0,"h":26.0,"text":"with","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":62.0,"y":96.0,"w":112.0,"h":26.0,"text":"decorator","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b3","x":192.0,"y":96.0,"w":112.0,"h":26.0,"text":"dataclass","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[15.6,26.6]}]},{"title":"Python idioms","sub":"Pythonic","short":"Idioms","main":"enumerate, zip, comprehensions, EAFP.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Unpacking and looping","Comprehensions and f-strings","EAFP"],"captions":["Unpacking instead of indexes, enumerate and zip instead of index loops, pathlib instead of joining paths","Comprehensions instead of manual accumulation, f-strings instead of adding strings, `is None` instead of `== None`","EAFP, \"easier to ask forgiveness\": t